{"user": "Why did I lose so badly?", "user_ts": "2026-08-12T21:52:29.402847+00:00", "assistant": "Final score looks like **White 44 \u2013 Black 20**.\n\nYou lost badly mainly because **White secured 3 corners**: **a1, h1, a8**, while Black only has **h8**. In Othello, corners are huge because they **can\u2019t be flipped back**, and they let your opponent safely build stable edges. Here White turned that into almost the entire **top edge, left edge, and bottom edge**.\n\nA common cause is playing squares **next to empty corners** too early \u2014 the \u201cdanger squares\u201d like **b1, a2, b2** near a1, etc. Those often give the opponent the corner later.\n\nAlso, in the endgame, winning is not about flipping the most discs on one move. It\u2019s about:\n- taking/denying **corners**\n- keeping **mobility** so opponent has bad/no moves\n- counting the final swing\n\nSo the short version: **White got stable corners and edges; Black\u2019s discs were mostly unstable and got swallowed in the final moves.**", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-12T21:52:29.402847+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-12T21:52:34.402847+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "consensus": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "votes": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 3}, "confidence": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 1.0}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "sonnet": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "llama": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle"], "consensus": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle"], "votes": {"Board Report": 3, "General Principle": 3, "Local Justification": 2}, "confidence": {"Board Report": 1.0, "General Principle": 1.0, "Local Justification": 0.6666666666666666}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Board Report", "General Principle"], "llama