{"user": "What exactly are X-squares? Never heard of that.", "user_ts": "2026-08-12T21:52:59.402847+00:00", "assistant": "**X-squares** are the 4 diagonal squares next to corners:\n\n- **b2** next to **a1**\n- **g2** next to **h1**\n- **b7** next to **a8**\n- **g7** next to **h8**\n\nThey\u2019re dangerous when the nearby corner is still empty, because playing there can give your opponent that corner.\n\nExample: if **a8** is empty and you play **b7**, White may later be able to take **a8**. Corners are permanent, so that\u2019s usually a big loss.\n\nIn your final board, White has **a8**, so if your **b7** let White take it, that explains a lot.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-12T21:52:59.402847+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-12T21:53:04.402847+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Knowledge Deficit Question", "Metacomment"], "consensus": ["Knowledge Deficit Question", "Metacomment"], "votes": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 3, "Metacomment": 2}, "confidence": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 1.0, "Metacomment": 0.6666666666666666}, "per_model": {"llama": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "gpt": ["Knowledge Deficit Question", "Metacomment"], "sonnet": ["Knowledge Deficit Question", "Metacomment"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle"], "consensus": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle"], "votes": {"Board Report": 3, "Local Justification": 3, "General Principle": 3}, "confidence": {"Board Report": 1.0, "Local Justification": 1.0, "General Principle": 1.0}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle"], "llama": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle"], "sonnet": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false, "coarse":